#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; for Administrators"
msgstr "KDE សម្រាប់​អ្នក​គ្រប់គ្រង"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; Internals"
msgstr "ខាងក្នុង KDE"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "ទិដ្ឋភាព​ទូទៅ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "to be written"
msgstr "ត្រូវ​បាន​សរសេរ"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory Layout"
msgstr "ប្លង់​ថត"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; defines a filesystem hierarchy which is used by the &kde; environment "
"itself as well as all &kde; applications. In general &kde; stores all its files "
"in a directory tree with a fixed structure."
msgstr ""
"KDE កំណត់​ថានានុក្រម​ប្រព័ន្ធ​ឯកសារ​ដែល​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដោយ​បរិស្ថាន​ខ្លួន​វា "
"រួម​ទាំង​កម្មវិធី KDE ទាំងអស់ ។ នៅ​ក្នុង KDE ទៅ​ទៅ "
"រក្សា​ឯកសារ​របស់​វា​ទាំងអស់​ក្នុង​មែកធាង​ថត​ជាមួយ​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ដែល​បាន​ជួសជុល "
"។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default &kde; uses two directory trees:"
msgstr "ដោយ​លំនាំ​ដើម KDE ប្រើ​មែកធាង​ថត​ពីរ ៖"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One at the system level (for example <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/opt/kde3</filename>)."
msgstr ""
"មួយ​នៅ​កម្រិត​ប្រព័ន្ធ (ឧទាហរណ៍ <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/opt/kde3</filename>) ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:41
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"One at the user level in the user's home directory (usually <filename "
"class=\"directory\"> ~/.kde</filename>)"
msgstr ""
"One at the user level in the user's home directory (usually <filename "
"class=\"directory\"> ~/.kde</filename>)"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As a system administrator you can create additional trees. Such additional "
"trees can be used for <link linkend=\"user-profiles\">profiles</link>"
msgstr ""
"As a system administrator you can create additional trees. Such additional "
"trees can be used for <link linkend=\"user-profiles\">profiles</link>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "&SuSE; &Linux; for example uses:"
msgstr "&SuSE; &Linux; for example uses:"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde"
msgstr "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>. (This is &SuSE;-specific; "
"other distributions may use <filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename> "
"or <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/kde3</filename>)"
msgstr ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename> ។ នេះ​គឺ​ស៊ូស៊ី​ជាក់លាក់ "
"ការ​ចែកចាយ​ផ្សេង​ទៀត​អាច​ប្រើ <filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename> "
"or <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/kde3</filename>)"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/etc/opt/kde3</filename>"
". (This was added by &SuSE;)."
msgstr ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/etc/opt/kde3</filename> "
"។ (នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​បន្ថែម​ដោយ ស៊ូស៊ី) ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have the KIOSK Admin tool v0.7 or later installed you can check which "
"directory trees are used with the following command: <userinput><command>"
"kiosktool-kdedirs</command> <option>--check</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""
"បើ​អ្នក​មាន​ឧបករណ៍​គ្រប់គ្រង KIOSK v0.7 ឬ ក្រោយ​បាន​ដំឡើង "
"អ្នក​អាច​ពិនិត្យ​មែកធាង​ថត​មួយ​ណា​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ជាមួយ​ពាក្យ​បញ្ជា​ខាងក្រោម ៖ "
"<userinput><command>kiosktool-kdedirs</command> <option>--check</option>"
"</userinput>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; and &kde; applications look up files by scanning all the &kde; directory "
"trees. The directory trees are checked in order of precedence. When a file is "
"present in multiple directory trees, the file from the last tree takes "
"precedence. Normally, the tree located in the user's home directory has the "
"highest precedence. This is also the directory tree to which changes are "
"written."
msgstr ""
"KDE និង​កម្មវិធី KDE រក​ឯកសារ​ដោយ​ស្គែន​មែកធាង​ថត KDE ទាំងអស់ ។ "
"មែកធាង​ថត​ត្រូវ​បាន​ធីក​ដើម្បី​ធ្វើ​អាទិភាព ។ "
"ពេល​ឯកសារ​ត្រូវ​បាន​បង្ហាញ​មែកធាង​ថត​ច្រើន ឯកសារ​ពី​មែកធាង​មុន​ចាប់​យក​អាទិភាព "
"។ ជា​ធម្មតា "
"មែកធាង​ដែល​មាន​ទីតាំង​ក្នុង​ថត​ផ្ទះ​របស់​អ្នក​ប្រើ​មាន​អាទិភាព​ខ្ពស់ ។ "
"នេះ​គឺ​ជា​មែកធាង​ថត​ដែល​ការ​ផ្លាស់ប្ដូរ​ត្រូវ​បាន​សរសេរ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For information about the <literal>text/plain</literal> "
"&MIME; type the following files are searched:"
msgstr ""
"សម្រាប់​ព័ត៌មាន​បន្ថែម​អំពី​ប្រភេទ <literal>text/plain</literal> "
"MIME ឯកសារ​ខាងក្រោម​ត្រូវ​បាន​ស្វែងរក ៖"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr "/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"
msgstr "/etc/opt/kde3/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a user makes a change, the change is written to <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop</"
"filename>"
msgstr ""
"បើ​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ធ្វើការ​ផ្លាស់ប្ដូរ ការ​ផ្លាស់ប្ដូរ​ត្រូវ​បាន​សរសេរ​ទៅ <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/mimelnk/text/plain.desktop</"
"filename>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For configuration files the story is slightly different. If there are multiple "
"configuration files found in the directory trees with the same name, their "
"content is combined. The precedence order of the directory trees plays a role "
"here. When two files define the same configuration key, the file with the "
"highest precedence determines which value is used for the key."
msgstr ""
"For configuration files the story is slightly different. If there are multiple "
"configuration files found in the directory trees with the same name, their "
"content is combined. The precedence order of the directory trees plays a role "
"here. When two files define the same configuration key, the file with the "
"highest precedence determines which value is used for the key."

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example, if the following two files exist, with these contents:"
msgstr "ឧទាហរណ៍ បើ​ឯកសារ​ខាងក្រោម​ពីរ​មាន ជាមួយ​មាតិកា​ទាំងនេះ ៖"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar"
msgstr "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle"
msgstr ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar"
msgstr "/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "The files will be merged to result in:"
msgstr "ឯកសារ​នឹង​ត្រូវ​បាន​បញ្ចូល​គ្នា​ជា​លទ្ធផល​ក្នុត ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifying Directories"
msgstr "ថត​ដែល​បញ្ជាក់"

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "Environment Variable"
msgstr "អថេរ​បរិស្ថាន"

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example Setting(s)"
msgstr "ឧទាហរណ៍​ការ​កំណត់"

#. Tag: segtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Comment"
msgstr "មតិយោបល់"

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEHOME"
msgstr "KDEHOME"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "~/.kde"
msgstr "~/.kde"

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEROOTHOME"
msgstr "KDEROOTHOME"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "/root/.kde"
msgstr "/root/.kde"

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Different variable to prevent root writing to $KDEHOME of the user after "
"running <command>su</command>."
msgstr ""
"អថេរ​ខុសគ្នា​ដើម្បី​ការពារ root មិន​ឲ្យ​សរសេរ​ទៅ $KDEHOME របស់​អ្នក​ប្រើ "
"បន្ទាប់​ពី​រត់ <command>su</command> ។"

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEDIR"
msgstr "KDEDIR"

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:150 kde-for-admins.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>, <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/usr/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde3</filename>, <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/usr/kde3</filename>"

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Vendor dependent. Used by &kde; 2. If not set, falls back to compiled-in "
"default."
msgstr ""
"ភាព​អាស្រ័យ​អ្នក​លក់ ។ ដែល​ប្រើ​ដោយ KDE ២ ។ បើ​មិន​កំណត់ "
"ធ្លាក់​ទៅ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ចងក្រង​ក្នុង​លំនាំ​ដើម ។"

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid "KDEDIRS"
msgstr "KDEDIRS"

#. Tag: seg
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"New in &kde;3. Can list multiple locations separated by a colon. If not set, "
"falls back to $<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
msgstr ""
"ថ្មី​ក្នុង KDE ៣ ។ អាច​រាយ​បញ្ជី​ទីតាំង​ច្រើន​ដែល​បំបែក​ដោយ​សញ្ញា (:) ។ "
"បើ​មិន​កំណត់ ត្រឡប់​ទៅ $<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Don't <emphasis>need</emphasis> to be set, defaults work just fine."
msgstr "មិន <emphasis>ត្រូវការ</emphasis> ឲ្យ​កំណត់ លំនាំ​ដើម​ធ្វើការ​ល្អ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Running &kde;2 next to &kde;3? Point $<envar>KDEDIR</envar> "
"to &kde; 2 and $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> to &kde; 3."
msgstr ""
"កំពុង​រត់ KDE ២ បន្ទាប់​ពី KDE ៣? ចង្អុល $<envar>KDEDIR</envar> "
"ទៅ KDE ២ និង $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> ទៅ KDE ៣ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid "A staff member at a university could have the following settings:"
msgstr "បុគ្គលិក​នៅ​សាកលវិទ្យាល័យ​អាច​មាន​ការ​កំណត់​ដូច​ខាងក្រោម ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"KDEHOME='~/.kde3'\n"
"KDEROOTHOME='/root/.kde3'\n"
"KDEDIRS='/opt/kde_staff:/opt/kde3'"
msgstr ""
"KDEHOME='~/.kde3'\n"
"KDEROOTHOME='/root/.kde3'\n"
"KDEDIRS='/opt/kde_staff:/opt/kde3'"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "User Profiles"
msgstr "ទម្រង់​អ្នក​ប្រើ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the previous example <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</filename> "
"contained additional settings and applications for staff members. <quote>"
"User Profiles</quote> allow you to add this directory only for certain users "
"and not for others. Add the following to <filename>/etc/kderc</filename>:"
msgstr ""
"នៅ​ក្នុង​ឧទាហរណ៍​មុន <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</filename> "
"ដែល​មាន​ការ​កំណត់​បន្ថែម និង​កម្មវិធី​សម្រាប់​បុគ្គលិក ។ <quote>"
"ទម្រង់​អ្នក​ប្រើ</quote> "
"អនុញ្ញាត​ឲ្យ​អ្នក​បន្ថែម​ថត​នេះ​តែ​សម្រាប់​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ដែល​មាន "
"និង​មិន​សម្រាប់​អ្នក​ផ្សេង​ទេ ។ បន្ថែម​ខាងក្រោម​ទៅ <filename>"
"/etc/kderc</filename> ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Directories-staff]\n"
"prefixes=/opt/kde_staff"
msgstr ""
"[Directories-staff]\n"
"prefixes=/opt/kde_staff"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This creates a profile named <quote>staff</quote> that adds the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</filename> directory tree. (Note that &SuSE; "
"&Linux; uses <filename>/etc/kde3rc</filename> instead of <filename>"
"/etc/kderc</filename>. Now that we have a named profile it can be assigned to "
"users."
msgstr ""
"នេះ​បង្កើតទម្រង់​ដែល​មាន​ឈ្មោះ <quote>staff</quote> ដែល​បន្ថែម​មែកធាង​ថត "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kde_staff</filename> "
"។  (ចំណាំ​ថា លីនុច ស៊ូស៊ី ប្រើ <filename>/etc/kde3rc</filename> ជំនួស <filename>"
"/etc/kderc</filename> ។ ឥឡូវ ពួក​យើង​មាន​ទម្រង់​ដែល​ដាក់​ឈ្មោះ "
"វា​អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ផ្ដល់​ទៅ​អ្នក​ប្រើ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To map profiles to users a mapping file needs to be specified in <filename>"
"/etc/kderc</filename>:"
msgstr ""
"ដើម្បី​ផ្គូផ្គង​ឯកសារ​ទៅ​អ្នក​ប្រើ "
"ឯកសារ​ដែល​ផ្គូផ្គង​ត្រូវការ​ឲ្យ​បញ្ជាក់​ក្នុង <filename>/etc/kderc</filename> ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Directories]\n"
"userProfileMapFile=/etc/kde-user-profile"
msgstr ""
"[Directories]\n"
"userProfileMapFile=/etc/kde-user-profile"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is now possible to assign a profile based on either the user name or based "
"on the &UNIX; group the user is part of."
msgstr ""
"ឥឡូវ​នេះ​អាច​ផ្ដល់​ទម្រង់​ដែល​មាន​មូលដ្ឋាន​នៅ​លើ​ឈ្មោះ​អ្នក​ប្រើ "
"ឬ​ដែល​មាន​មូលដ្ឋាន​លើ​ក្រុម យូនីក ដែល​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ជា​ផ្នែក​របស់ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:207
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To assign the staff profile to all users that are a member of the &UNIX; group "
"staff_members add the following to <filename>/etc/kde-user-profile</filename>:"
msgstr ""
"ដើម្បី​ផ្ដល់​ទម្រង់​បុគ្គលិក​ទៅ​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ទាំងអស់​ដែល​ជា​បុគ្គលិក​របស់​ក្រុម "
"យូនីក staff_members បន្ថែម​ខាងក្រោម​ទៅ "
"<filename>/etc/kde-user-profile</filename> ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[General]\n"
"groups=staff_members\n"
"[Groups]\n"
"staff_members=staff"
msgstr ""
"[General]\n"
"groups=staff_members\n"
"[Groups]\n"
"staff_members=staff"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "It is also possible to assign a profile to a single user:"
msgstr "វា​អាច​ផ្ដល់​ទម្រង់​ទៅ​អ្នក​ប្រើ​តែ​មួយ ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Users]\n"
"bastian=staff"
msgstr ""
"[Users]\n"
"bastian=staff"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory Layout Revisited"
msgstr "ប្លង់​ថត​ដែល​បាន​ទស្សនា​ឡើង​វិញ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each directory tree used by &kde; has a fixed directory structure. Directories "
"that are not relevant for a certain tree, or simply not used can be left out "
"though. For example, directories used for temporary files are usually only "
"found under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar></filename> "
"but not in any other directory tree."
msgstr ""
"មែកធាង​ថត​នីមួយ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដោយ KDE មាន​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ថត​ដែល​បាន​ជួសជយល ។ "
"ថត​ដែល​មិន​ទាក់ទង​សម្រាប់​មែកធាង​ជាក់លាក់ ឬ​ជា​ធម្មតា​មិន​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ "
"អាច​ទុក​ចោល ។ ឧទាហរណ៍ "
"ថត​ដែល​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់​ឯកសារ​បណ្ដោះ​អាសន្ន​ជានិច្ចជាកាល​រក​ឃើញ​នៅ​ពី​ក្រោម "
"<filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar></filename> "
"ប៉ុន្តែ​មិន​នៅ​ក្នុង​មែកធាង​ថត​ផ្សេង​ណា​មួយ​ទេ ។"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Architecture-specific Directories"
msgstr "ថត​ស្ថាបត្យកម្ម​ជាក់លាក់"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Architecture (OS and CPU type) specific directories:"
msgstr "ថត​ស្ថាបត្យកម្ម​ជាក់លាក់ (ប្រភេទ OS និង CPU) ៖"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>bin</filename>"
msgstr "<filename>bin</filename>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid "Used for &kde; executables."
msgstr "ដែល​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់ KDE ដែល​អាច​ប្រតិបត្តិ ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>lib</filename>"
msgstr "<filename>lib</filename>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Used for &kde; libraries."
msgstr "ដែល​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់​បណ្ណាល័យ KDE ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "lib/kde3"
msgstr "lib/kde3"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains components, plugins, and other runtime loadable objects "
"for use by &kde; 3.<replaceable>x</replaceable> applications."
msgstr ""
"ថត​នេះ​មាន​សមាសភាគ កម្មវិធី​ជំនួយ "
"និង​ពេល​វេលា​វត្ថុ​ដែល​អាច​ផ្ទុក​បាន​សម្រាប់​ប្រើ​ដោយ KDE ៣ ។ កម្មវិធី "
"<replaceable>x</replaceable> ។"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shared Directories"
msgstr "ថត​ដែល​បាន​ចែក​រំលែក"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Shared: Not architecture specific, can be shared between different archs."
msgstr ""
"ដែល​បាន​ចែក​រំលែក ៖ មិន​មែន​ជា​ស្ថាបត្យកម្ម​ជាក់លាក់ "
"អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ចែក​រំលែក​រវាង archs ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:266
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/applnk"
msgstr "share/applnk"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files for &kde;-menu (old)"
msgstr ""
"ឯកសារ <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> សម្រាប់ kde-menu (ចាស់)"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/applications"
msgstr "share/applications"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:273
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files for &kde;-menu (since "
"&kde; 3.2)"
msgstr ""
"ឯកសារ <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"សម្រាប់ kde-menu (តាំង​ពី KDE ៣.២)"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/apps"
msgstr "share/apps"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Contains application-specific data files. Each application has a sub-directory "
"here for storing additional data files."
msgstr ""
"មាន​ឯកសារ​ទិន្នន័យ​កម្មវិធី​ជាក់លាក់ ។ "
"កម្មវិធី​នីមួយៗ​មាន​ថត​រង​ទីនេះ​សម្រាប់​រក្សា​ឯកសារ​ទិន្នន័យ​បន្ថែម ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/config"
msgstr "share/config"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configuration files. Configuration files are normally named after the "
"application they belong to plus the letters <quote>rc</quote>"
". A special case is <filename>kdeglobals</filename>. This file is read by all "
"&kde; applications."
msgstr ""
"ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ ។ "
"ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ជា​ធម្មតា​ត្រូវ​បាន​ដាក់​ឈ្មោះ​តាម​កម្មវិធី "
"ដែល​ពួក​វា​ជា​កម្មសិទ្ធិ​ទៅ​និង​តួអក្សរ + <quote>rc</quote> "
"។ ករណី​ពិសេស​គឺ <filename>kdeglobals</filename> ។ "
"ឯកសារ​នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​អាន​ដោយ​កម្មវិធី KDE ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/config/session"
msgstr "share/config/session"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory is used by session management and is normally only available "
"under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar></filename>"
". At the end of a session &kde; applications store their state here. The file "
"names consist of the name of the application followed by a number. The session "
"manager <command>ksmserver</command> stores references to these numbers when "
"saving a session in <filename>ksmserverrc</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/doc/HTML"
msgstr "share/doc/HTML"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains documentation for &kde; applications. Documentation is "
"categorized by language and the application it belongs to. Normally at least "
"two files can be found in a directory: <filename>index.docbook</filename>"
", which contains the documentation in the unformatted DocBook format, and "
"<filename>index.cache.bz2</filename>, which contains the same documentation "
"formatted as <command>bzip2</command>-compressed &HTML;. The &HTML; version is "
"used by &khelpcenter;. If the &HTML; version is missing, &khelpcenter; will "
"regenerate it from the DocBook version but this is a time-consuming process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/icons"
msgstr "share/icons"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under this directory icons are stored. Icons are categorized by theme, "
"dimension and usage category."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/mimelnk"
msgstr "share/mimelnk"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this directory,<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"files that describe &MIME; types are stored. &kde; uses &MIME; types to "
"identify the type of a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/services"
msgstr "share/services"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:338
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"files that describe services. Services are like applications but are usually "
"launched by other applications instead of the user. Services do not appear in "
"the &kde; menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/servicetypes"
msgstr "share/servicetypes"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"files that describe servicetypes. A servicetype usually represents a certain "
"programming interface. Applications and Services include in their <literal "
"role=\"extension\">>.desktop</literal> files the servicetypes that they "
"provide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/sounds"
msgstr "share/sounds"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid "This directory contains sound files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/templates"
msgstr "share/templates"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:361
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This directory contains templates for creating files of various types. A "
"template consists of a <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"file that describes the file and that includes a reference to a file in the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">.source</filename> sub-directory. The templates "
"in this directory appear in the <guimenu>Create New</guimenu> "
"menu available on the desktop and in the file browser. When a user selects a "
"template from the menu its source file is copied."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "share/wallpapers"
msgstr "share/wallpapers"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:374
#, no-c-format
msgid "This directory contains images that can be used as background picture"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid "Host-specific Directories"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three host-specific directories that are usually symlinked to other "
"locations. If the directories do not already exist, the following symlinks and "
"directories will be created using the <command>lnusertemp</command> utility:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/socket-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/socket-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/ksocket-$<envar>USER</envar>"
"/</filename>, this is used for various &UNIX; sockets."
msgstr ""
"ជា​ធម្មតា <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/ksocket-$<envar>USER</envar>"
"/</filename> នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់​រន្ធ យូនីក ផ្សេងៗ ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/tmp-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/tmp-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:402
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/kde-$<envar>USER</envar>/</filename>"
", this is used for temporary files."
msgstr ""
"ជា​ធម្មតា <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/kde-$<envar>USER</envar>"
"/</filename>, នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់​ឯកសារ​បណ្ដោះ​អាសន្ន ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/cache-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/cache-$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp/kdecache-$<envar>USER</envar>"
"/</filename>, this is used for cached files."
msgstr ""
"ជា​ធម្មតា <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp/kdecache-$<envar>USER</envar>"
"/</filename> នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់​ឯកសារ​ដែល​ដាក់​ក្នុង​ឃ្លាំង​សម្ងាត់ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since both <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp</filename> "
"and <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp</filename> "
"are world writable, there is a possibility that one of the above directories "
"already exists but is owned by another user. In that case the <command>"
"lnusertemp</command> utility will create a new directory with an alternative "
"name and link to that instead."
msgstr ""
"ពីព្រោះ​ទាំង <filename class=\"directory\">/tmp</filename> "
"និង <filename class=\"directory\">/var/tmp</filename> "
"ជា​ប្រភព​ដែល​អាច​សរសេរ​បាន មាន​លទ្ធភាព​ដែល​ថត​ខាង​លើ​មួយ​មាន​រួច​ហើយ "
"ប៉ុន្តែ​ជា​ម្ចាស់​ដោយ​អ្នក​ប្រើ​ផ្សេង​ទៀត ។ ក្នុង​ករណី​នោះ​ឧបករណ៍​ប្រើប្រាស់ "
"<command>lnusertemp</command> នឹង​បង្កើត​ថត​ថ្មី​ជាមួយ​ឈ្មោះ​ដែល​ដូច "
"និង​តភ្ជាប់​ទៅ​នោះ​ជំនួស ។"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Files"
msgstr "ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; uses a simple text-based file format for all its configuration files. It "
"consists of key-value pairs that are placed in groups. All &kde; configuration "
"files use <acronym>UTF</acronym>-8 encoding for text outside the <acronym>"
"ASCII</acronym> range."
msgstr ""
"KDE "
"ប្រើ​ឯកសារ​ដែល​ផ្អែក​លើ​អត្ថបទ​ធម្មតា​សម្រាប់​ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ធម្ម"
"តា ។ វា​មាន​គូ​តម្លៃ​គ្រាប់ចុច​ដែល​ត្រូវ​បាន​ដាក់​ជា​ក្រុម ។ "
"ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ទាំងអស់ KDE ប្រើ​សំណុំ​តួ​អក្សរ <acronym>"
"UTF</acronym>-8 សម្រាប់​អត្ថបទ​ខាងក្រៅ​ជួរ <acronym>ASCII</acronym> ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The start of a group is indicated by a group name that is placed in square "
"brackets. All the key-value entries that follow belong to the group. The group "
"ends when either another group starts or when the end of the file is reached. "
"Entries at the top of the file that are not preceded by a group name belong to "
"the default group."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following example shows a configuration file that consists of two groups. "
"The first group contains the keys <varname>LargeCursor</varname> and <varname>"
"SingleClick</varname>, the second group contains the keys <varname>"
"Show hidden files</varname> and <varname>Sort by</varname>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE]\n"
"LargeCursor=false\n"
"SingleClick=true"
msgstr ""
"[KDE]\n"
"LargeCursor=false\n"
"SingleClick=true"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KFileDialog Settings]\n"
"Show hidden files=false\n"
"Sort by=Name"
msgstr ""
"[KFileDialog Settings]\n"
"Show hidden files=false\n"
"Sort by=Name"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entries in a group consist of a key and value separated by an equals sign. The "
"key can contain spaces and may be followed by options placed in square "
"brackets. The part after the equals sign is the value of the entry. Any white "
"space surrounding the equals sign is ignored, as is any trailing white space. "
"Put more concisely, the format is:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid "<replaceable>entry</replaceable>=<replaceable>value</replaceable>"
msgstr "<replaceable>entry</replaceable>=<replaceable>value</replaceable>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a value is supposed to include a space at the begin or end then this can be "
"achieved by using a backslash followed by an <quote>s</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:462
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are several other backslash codes; here is a complete list:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\s</token> can be used as space"
msgstr "<token>\\s</token> អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ជា​ដក​ឃ្លា"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:467
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\t</token> can be used to include a tab"
msgstr "<token>\\t</token> អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​បញ្ចូល ថេប"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:469
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\r</token> for a carriage return character"
msgstr "<token>\\r</token> សម្រាប់​ដឹក​ជញ្ជូន​តួ​អក្សរ​ត្រឡប់"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<token>\\n</token> for a linefeed character (new line)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "<token>\\\\</token> to include the backslash itself"
msgstr "<token>\\\\</token> ដើម្បី​បញ្ចូល​សញ្ញា \\ ខ្លួន​វា"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> "
"entry starts with two spaces while the <varname>Description</varname> "
"entry contains three lines of text. Linefeeds in backslash notation are used to "
"separate the different lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=\\s My Caption\n"
"Description=This is\\na very long\\ndescription."
msgstr ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=\\s My Caption\n"
"Description=This is\\na very long\\ndescription."

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Empty lines in configuration files are ignored, as are lines that start with a "
"hash mark (<quote>#</quote>). The hash mark can be used to add comments to "
"configuration files. It should be noted that when a &kde; application updates a "
"configuration file the comments are <emphasis>not</emphasis> preserved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There can be multiple configuration files with the same name in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">share/config</filename> sub-directory of the various &kde; "
"directory trees. In this case the information of all these configuration files "
"is combined on a key-by-key basis. If the same key within a certain group is "
"defined in more than one place, the key value read from the directory tree with "
"the highest precedence will be used. Configuration files under <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar></filename> "
"always have the highest precedence. If a key in a certain group is defined "
"multiple times in a single file, the value of the last entry is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""
"បើ <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន ៖ <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> និង <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"និង <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> លទ្ធផល​នឹង​ជា ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:510
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=10,10"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Position=20,20\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""
"បើ <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"</programlisting> និង <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Position=20,20\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> លទ្ធផល​នឹង​ជា ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=20,20"
msgstr ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=green\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"Position=20,20"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To prevent users being able to override default settings, settings can be "
"marked immutable. Settings can be made immutable individually, per group or per "
"file. An individual entry can be locked down by adding <userinput>"
"[$i]</userinput> behind the key, &eg;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "Color[$i]=blue"
msgstr "Color[$i]=blue"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A group of entries can be locked down by placing <userinput>[$i]</userinput> "
"behind the group name, &eg;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:536
#, no-c-format
msgid "[MyGroup][$i]"
msgstr "[MyGroup][$i]"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To lock down the entire file, start the file with <userinput>[$i]</userinput> "
"on a single line, &ie;:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:540
#, no-c-format
msgid "[$i]"
msgstr "[$i]"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be:"
msgstr ""
"បើ <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន ៖ <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> និង <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន ៖ <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> លទ្ធផល​នឹង​ជា ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains: <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> the result will be"
msgstr ""
"បើ <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន ៖ <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=red\n"
"Shape=circle\n"
"</programlisting> and <filename>/opt/kde_staff/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"</programlisting> និង <filename>/etc/opt/kde3/share/config/foobar</filename> "
"មាន <programlisting>\n"
"[MyGroup][$i]\n"
"Color=blue\n"
"Position=10,10\n"
"</programlisting> លទ្ធផល​នឹង​ជា"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"Position=10,10"
msgstr ""
"[MyGroup]\n"
"Color=purple\n"
"Shape=rectangle\n"
"Position=10,10"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:569
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"So-called <quote>Shell Expansion</quote> can be used to provide more dynamic "
"default values. With shell expansion the value of a configuration key can be "
"constructed from the value of an environment variable or from the output of a "
"shell command. To enable shell expansion for a configuration entry, the key "
"must be followed by <token>[$e]</token>. Normally the expanded form is written "
"into the user's configuration file after first use. To prevent that, it is "
"recommend to lock the configuration entry down by using <token>[$ie]</token>"
". The user can't change it then of course."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:579
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value for the <varname>Host</varname> "
"entry is determined by the output of the <command>hostname</command> "
"program. This setting is also locked down to ensure that the value is always "
"determined dynamically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The value for the <varname>Email</varname> entry is determined by filling in "
"the values of the $<envar>USER</envar> and $<envar>HOST</envar> "
"environment variables. When <systemitem class=\"username\">joe</systemitem> "
"is logged in on <systemitem class=\"systemname\">joes_host</systemitem> "
"this will result in a value equal to <literal>joe@joes_host</literal>"
". The setting is not locked down."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:591
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Mail Settings] \n"
"Host[$ie]=$(hostname)\n"
"Email[$e]=${USER}@${HOST}"
msgstr ""
"[Mail Settings] \n"
"Host[$ie]=$(hostname)\n"
"Email[$e]=${USER}@${HOST}"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most configuration entries can be indexed with a language code. In this case, "
"the language that the user has selected for use on the desktop is used to look "
"up the key value. If the default language (American English) has been selected "
"or if there is no index that corresponds to the selected language, the key "
"entry without index is used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:601
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the following example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> "
"entry depends on the language. If the user has selected French as language "
"(language code <literal>fr</literal>) the value of the entry will be <quote>"
"Ma L&eacute;gende</quote>. In all other cases the value <quote>"
"My Caption</quote> will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:607 kde-for-admins.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=My Caption\n"
"Caption[fr]=Ma L&eacute;gende"
msgstr ""
"[Preview Image]\n"
"Caption=My Caption\n"
"Caption[fr]=Ma L&eacute;gende"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this example the value of the <varname>Caption</varname> "
"entry depends on the language. If the user has selected French as language "
"(language code <literal>fr</literal>) the value of the entry will be <quote>"
"Ma L&eacute;gende.</quote> In all other cases the value <quote>"
"My Caption</quote> will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In general the entries that can appear in a configuration file are not "
"documented. With &kde; 3.2 a start has been made to change this. In <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config.kcfg</filename>"
", files can be found that provide a formal description of the possible entries "
"in a configuration file. These are used by the new &kde; Configuration Editor "
"when available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:629
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is an example &XML; configuration file:"
msgstr "នេះ​គឺ​ជា​ឧទាហរណ៍​ឯកសារ​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ XML ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<markup>\n"
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?&gt;\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE kcfg SYSTEM "
"\"http://www.kde.org/standards/kcfg/1.0/kcfg.dtd\"&gt;\n"
"&lt;kcfg&gt;\n"
"    &lt;kcfgfile name=\"korganizerrc\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;group name=\"General\"&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Bool\" key=\"Auto Save\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;label&gt;Enable automatic saving of calendar&lt;/label&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;true&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Int\" key=\"Auto Save Interval\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;10&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"&lt;/kcfg&gt;\n"
"</markup>"
msgstr ""
"<markup>\n"
"&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?&gt;\n"
"&lt;!DOCTYPE kcfg SYSTEM "
"\"http://www.kde.org/standards/kcfg/1.0/kcfg.dtd\"&gt;\n"
"&lt;kcfg&gt;\n"
"    &lt;kcfgfile name=\"korganizerrc\"/&gt;\n"
"    &lt;group name=\"General\"&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Bool\" key=\"Auto Save\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;label&gt;Enable automatic saving of calendar&lt;/label&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;true&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"         &lt;entry type=\"Int\" key=\"Auto Save Interval\"&gt;\n"
"             &lt;default&gt;10&lt;/default&gt;\n"
"         &lt;/entry&gt;\n"
"    &lt;/group&gt;\n"
"&lt;/kcfg&gt;\n"
"</markup>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "It has the same effect as:"
msgstr "វា​មាន​បែបផែន​ដូច ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[General]\n"
"Auto Save=false\n"
"Auto Save Interval=25"
msgstr ""
"[General]\n"
"Auto Save=false\n"
"Auto Save Interval=25"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; Startup Sequence"
msgstr "លំដាប់​ចាប់ផ្ដើម KDE"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kdm;"
msgstr "Kdm"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:645
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Always runs as <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>! Uses <filename>"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdmrc</filename> and <filename>"
"/etc/X11/xdm/Xservers</filename>. The latter contains entries like:"
msgstr ""
"រត់​ជានិច្ច​ជា <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>! ប្រើ <filename>"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/config/kdmrc</filename> និង <filename>"
"/etc/X11/xdm/Xservers</filename> ។ តួ​អក្សរ​មាន​ធាតុ​ដូចជា ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:650
#, no-c-format
msgid ":0 local /usr/X11R6/bin/X :0 vt07"
msgstr ":0 local /usr/X11R6/bin/X :0 vt07"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "Relevant startup files are also:"
msgstr "ឯកសារ​ចាប់ផ្ដើម​ជាប់ទាក់​គឺ ៖"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:654
#, no-c-format
msgid "[X-*-Core] section in <filename>kdmrc</filename>"
msgstr "ការ​ជ្រើស [X-*-Core] នៅ​ក្នុង <filename>kdmrc</filename>"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setup - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsetup</filename>"
msgstr "រៀបចំ - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsetup</filename>"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "User enters username &amp; password"
msgstr "អ្នក​ប្រើ​បញ្ចូល​ឈ្មោះ​អ្នក​ប្រើ &amp; ពាក្យ​សម្ងាត់"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid "Startup - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xstartup</filename> - prepare as root"
msgstr "ចាប់ផ្ដើម - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xstartup</filename> - រៀបចំ​ជា root"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Session - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsession</filename> - starts session as user"
msgstr ""
"សម័យ - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xsession</filename> - ចាប់ផ្ដើម​សម័យ​ជា​អ្នក​ប្រើ"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"= For a KDE session: <command>kde</command> or <command>startkde</command>"
msgstr ""
"= សម្រាប់​សម័យ KDE ៖ <command>kde</command> ឬ <command>startkde</command>"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:672
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"= If present <filename>~/.xsession</filename> or <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>"
msgstr ""
"= បើ​បង្ហាញ <filename>~/.xsession</filename> ឬ <filename>~/.xinitrc</filename>"

#. Tag: member
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reset - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xreset</filename> - after session finished"
msgstr ""
"កំណត់​ឡើង​វិញ - <filename>/etc/X11/xdm/Xreset</filename> "
"- បន្ទាប់​ពី​សម័យ​បាន​បញ្ចប់"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:683
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Startup Script: <command>startkde</command>"
msgstr "ស្គ្រីប​ចាប់ផ្ដើម KDE ៖ <command>startkde</command>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:685
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; startup sequence starts with the <filename>startkde</filename> "
"script. In most cases this script gets called from the display manager (&kdm;) "
"once the user has been authenticated. Their are two very important lines in the "
"<filename>startkde</filename> script:"
msgstr ""
"លំដាប់​ចាប់ផ្ដើម KDE ចាប់ផ្ដើម​ជាមួយ​ស្គ្រីប <filename>startkde</filename> "
"។ នៅ​ក្នុង​ករណី​ជា​ច្រើន "
"ស្គ្រីប​នេះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ហៅ​ពី​កម្មវិធី​គ្រប់គ្រង​ការ​បង្ហាញ (Kdm) "
"ពេល​អ្នក​ប្រើ​បាន​ត្រូវ​ផ្ទៀងផ្ទាត់​ភាព​ត្រឹមត្រូវ ។ "
"មាន​បន្ទាត់​សំខាន់​ពីរ​នៅ​ក្នុង​ស្គ្រីប <filename>startkde</filename> ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:691
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"LD_BIND_NOW=true kdeinit +kcminit +knotify and kwrapper\n"
"ksmserver $KDEWM"
msgstr ""
"LD_BIND_NOW=true kdeinit +kcminit +knotify and kwrapper\n"
"ksmserver $KDEWM"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first line starts the <command>kdeinit</command> "
"master process. The <command>kdeinit</command> master process is used to start "
"all other &kde; processes. It show up in the output of <command>ps <option>"
"aux</option></command> as <computeroutput>kdeinit: Running...</computeroutput>"
". The arguments after <command>kdeinit</command> are the names of additional "
"processes to be started. The <token>+</token> indicates that <command>"
"kdeinit</command> needs to wait till the process has finished. <command>"
"kdeinit</command> also starts <command>dcopserver</command>, <command>"
"klauncher</command> and <command>kded</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The second of the two lines asks <command>kdeinit</command> "
"to start the <command>ksmserver</command> session manager process. The session "
"manager determines the lifetime of the session. When this process exits, the "
"user is logged out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:713
#, no-c-format
msgid "Background Processes"
msgstr "ដំណើរ​ការ​ផ្ទៃ​ខាងក្រោយ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:715
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All &kde; background services are user-specific: unlike system daemons they are "
"not shared between users. As well as being unique per user they are also unique "
"per X-server display. The processes are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:721 kde-for-admins.docbook:797
#, no-c-format
msgid "dcopserver"
msgstr "dcopserver"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid "Desktop communication"
msgstr "ទំនាក់ទំនង​ផ្ទៃតុ"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:727
#, no-c-format
msgid "kded"
msgstr "Kded"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:728
#, no-c-format
msgid "Generic service daemon."
msgstr "ដេមិន​សេវា​ប្រភេទ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Triggers <link linkend=\"ksycoca\">Sycoca</link> database updates when needed"
msgstr ""
"កេះ​ភាព​ទាន់​សម័យ​មូលដ្ឋាន​ទិន្នន័យ <link linkend=\"ksycoca\">Sycoca</link> "
"ពេល​ត្រូវការ"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kcminit</command>"
msgstr "<command>kcminit</command>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:736
#, no-c-format
msgid "Initialization service"
msgstr "សេវា​ការ​ចាប់ផ្ដើម"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"kcminit\"/> for more information."
msgstr "សូម​មើល <xref linkend=\"kcminit\"/> សម្រាប់​ព័ត៌មាន​បន្ថែម ។"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:742 kde-for-admins.docbook:853
#, no-c-format
msgid "klauncher"
msgstr "Klauncher"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Program launch (this is <emphasis>not</emphasis> the <keycombo action=\"simul\">"
"&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap> </keycombo>dialog!)"
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​បើក​ដំណើរ​ការ (នេះ​គឺ <emphasis>មិន​មែន</emphasis> "
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">ប្ដូរ(Alt)<keycap>F2</keycap> </keycombo>dialog!)"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"klauncher\"/> for more information."
msgstr "សូម​មើល <xref linkend=\"klauncher\"/> សម្រាប់​ព័ត៌មាន​បន្ថែម ៖"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:751 kde-for-admins.docbook:874
#, no-c-format
msgid "knotify"
msgstr "Knotify"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid "User notifications."
msgstr "ការ​ជូន​ដំណឹង​អ្នក​ប្រើ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"knotify\"/> for more information."
msgstr "សូម​មើល <xref linkend=\"knotify\"/> សម្រាប់​ព័ត៌មាន​បន្ថែម ។"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:758
#, no-c-format
msgid "ksmserver"
msgstr "Ksmserver"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "Session management"
msgstr "ការ​គ្រប់គ្រង​សម័យ"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid "See <xref linkend=\"ksmserver\"/> for more information."
msgstr "សូម​មើល <xref linkend=\"ksmserver\"/> សម្រាប់​ព័ត៌មាន​បន្ថែម ។"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdeinit"
msgstr "Kdeinit"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdeinit</command> is used to start all other &kde; programs. <command>"
"kdeinit</command> can start normal binary program files as well as <command>"
"kdeinit</command> loadable modules (<acronym>KLM</acronym>s). <acronym>"
"KLM</acronym>s work just like binary program files but can be started more "
"efficiently. <acronym>KLM</acronym>s live in <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/lib/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<command>kdeinit</command> ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​ចាប់ផ្ដើម​កម្មវិធី KDE ។ "
"<command>kdeinit</command> អាច​ចាប់ផ្ដើម​ឯកសារ​កម្មវិធី​ប្រព័ន្ធ​គោលពីរ​ធម្មតា "
"រួម​ទាំង​ម៉ូឌុល​ដែល​អាច​ផ្ទុក​បាន <command>kdeinit</command> (<acronym>"
"KLM</acronym>s) ។ <acronym>KLM</acronym> "
"ធ្វើការ​ដូច​ឯកសារ​កម្មវិធី​ប្រព័ន្ធ​គោលពីរ "
"ប៉ុន្តែ​អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ចាប់ផ្ដើម​យ៉ាង​មាន​ប្រសិទ្ធិភាព​ជាង ។ <acronym>"
"KLM</acronym> រស់​នៅ​ក្នុង <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
"/lib/kde3</filename>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:776 kde-for-admins.docbook:1163
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The drawback is that programs started this way appear as <computeroutput>"
"<command>kdeinit</command></computeroutput> in the output of <command>"
"top</command> and <command>ps</command>. Use <command>top <option>-c</option>"
"</command> or <command>ps <option>aux</option></command> "
"to see the actual program name:"
msgstr ""
"The drawback is that programs started this way appear as <computeroutput>"
"<command>kdeinit</command></computeroutput> in the output of <command>"
"top</command> and <command>ps</command>. Use <command>top <option>-c</option>"
"</command> or <command>ps <option>aux</option></command> "
"to see the actual program name:"

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt><userinput><command>ps <option>aux</option></command>"
"</userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"waba     23184  0.2  2.1 23428 11124 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"Running...\n"
"waba     23187  0.1  2.1 23200 11124 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"dcopserver --nosid\n"
"waba     23189  0.2  2.4 25136 12496 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klauncher\n"
"waba     23192  0.7  2.8 25596 14772 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: kded\n"
"waba     23203  0.8  3.4 31516 17892 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit:\n"
"knotify\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""
"<prompt>%</prompt><userinput><command>ps <option>aux</option></command>"
"</userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"waba     23184  0.2  2.1 23428 11124 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"Running...\n"
"waba     23187  0.1  2.1 23200 11124 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"dcopserver --nosid\n"
"waba     23189  0.2  2.4 25136 12496 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klauncher\n"
"waba     23192  0.7  2.8 25596 14772 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit: kded\n"
"waba     23203  0.8  3.4 31516 17892 ?        S    21:41   0:00 kdeinit:\n"
"knotify\n"
"</computeroutput>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<computeroutput>kdeinit: Running...</computeroutput> "
"indicates the master <command>kdeinit</command> process. The other processes "
"listed are programs started as <acronym>KLM</acronym>s."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:788
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When <command>kdeinit</command> starts for the first time it will launch "
"<command>dcopserver</command>, <command>klauncher</command>, and <command>"
"kded</command>, as well as any additional programs specified on its command "
"line in the <command>startkde</command> script, normally <command>"
"kcminit</command> and <command>knotify</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:799
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>dcopserver</command> is a daemon which provides inter-process "
"communication (&DCOP;) facilities to all &kde; applications. The &DCOP; "
"facilities are accessible from the command shell via the <command>dcop</command> "
"command line tool. &DCOP; is essential for all &kde; applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:805
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some related files:"
msgstr "ឯកសារ​ដែល​ជាប់​ទាក់ទង​ខ្លះ ៖"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:809
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.DCOPserver_$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>_$<envar>"
"DISPLAY</envar>"
msgstr ""
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.DCOPserver_$<envar>HOSTNAME</envar>_$<envar>"
"DISPLAY</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&eg; <filename>.DCOPserver_linux__0</filename>. Controlled by $<envar>"
"DCOPAUTHORITY</envar>"
msgstr ""
"ឧ. <filename>.DCOPserver_linux__0</filename> ។ ដែល​បញ្ជា​ដោយ $<envar>"
"DCOPAUTHORITY</envar>"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"/tmp/.ICE-unix/dcop<replaceable>pid</replaceable>-<replaceable>"
"number</replaceable>"
msgstr ""
"/tmp/.ICE-unix/dcop<replaceable>pid</replaceable>-<replaceable>"
"number</replaceable>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:816
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&eg; <filename>dcop7634-1069677856</filename>. This is the file that the "
"<filename>DCOPserver</filename> file above points to."
msgstr ""
"ឧ. <filename>dcop7634-1069677856</filename> ។ នេះ​គឺ​ជា​ឯកសារ​ដែល​ឯកសារ "
"<filename>DCOPserver</filename> លើ​ចំណុច ។"

#. Tag: filename
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:822
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.ICEauthority"
msgstr "$<envar>HOME</envar>/.ICEauthority"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:823
#, no-c-format
msgid "Authorization information controlled by $<envar>ICEAUTHORITY</envar>"
msgstr ""
"ព័ត៌មាន​ផ្ទៀងផ្ទាត់​ភាព​ត្រឹមត្រូវ​ដែល​បញ្ជា​ដោយ $<envar>ICEAUTHORITY</envar>"

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:832
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>kcminit</title>"
msgstr "<title>Kcminit</title>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kcminit</command> executes initialization services during startup. "
"Initialization services are specified in the .desktop files of applications or "
"services via the <varname>X-KDE-Init</varname> line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:838
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8\n"
"Exec=kcmshell energy\n"
"Icon=energy_star\n"
"Type=Application\n"
"X-KDE-Library=energy\n"
"X-KDE-Init=energy"
msgstr ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8\n"
"Exec=kcmshell energy\n"
"Icon=energy_star\n"
"Type=Application\n"
"X-KDE-Library=energy\n"
"X-KDE-Init=energy"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:840
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Initialization services are typically used for initializing hardware based on "
"user-specified settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:843
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kcminit <option>--list</option></command></userinput> "
"can be used to show all initialization services and <userinput><command>"
"kcminit <replaceable>service</replaceable></command></userinput> "
"can be used to execute a single service explicitly. This can be useful when "
"investigating startup problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:855
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>klauncher</command> is a daemon which is responsible for service "
"activation within &kde;. It operates in close connection with the <command>"
"kdeinit</command> master process to start new processes. &kde; applications "
"communicate with <command>klauncher</command> over &DCOP; in order to start new "
"applications or services."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:861
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Best known from the error message: <computeroutput><errortext> "
"KLauncher could not be reached via DCOP </errortext></computeroutput> "
"which either indicates a serious problem with the <command>dcopserver</command> "
"or that <command>klauncher</command> crashed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:866
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>klauncher</command> can be restarted by restarting <command>"
"kdeinit</command> from a console window. Make sure that $<envar>HOME</envar>"
", $<envar>DISPLAY</envar> and the various $<envar>KDEDIR(S)</envar> "
"are set correctly when doing so!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:876
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The primary task of <command>knotify</command> is to relay sound notifications "
"to the sound server, it also provides alternative notification methods."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid "KSMServer"
msgstr "KSMServer"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:888
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>ksmserver</command> is &kde;'s session manager. On startup the session "
"manager launches auto-start applications and restores applications from the "
"previous session. The applications to auto-start are indicated by <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> files in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/autostart</filename> "
"directory. Whether or not to auto-start an application can be made conditional "
"upon some configuration entry determined by the <varname>"
"X-KDE-autostart-condition</varname> entry in the <literal role=\"extension\">"
".desktop</literal> file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:900
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <filename>ktip.desktop</filename> file for example contains:"
msgstr "ឯកសារ <filename>ktip.desktop</filename> សម្រាប់​ឧទាហរណ៍​ដែល​មាន ៖"

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:903
#, no-c-format
msgid "X-KDE-autostart-condition=ktiprc:TipOfDay:RunOnStart:true"
msgstr "X-KDE-autostart-condition=ktiprc:TipOfDay:RunOnStart:true"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:905
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This means that the <filename>ktiprc</filename> configuration file is checked "
"for a <varname>RunOnStart</varname> entry in the <varname>[TipOfDay]</varname> "
"section. If no such entry is found, <literal>true</literal> "
"is assumed, which means that <application>ktip</application> "
"is one of the applications that is auto-started by default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of the applications auto-started by <command>ksmserver</command> are:"
msgstr ""
"កម្មវិធី​ខ្លះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ចាប់ផ្ដើម​ដោយ​ស្វ័យប្រវត្តិ​ដោយ <command>"
"ksmserver</command> គឺ ៖"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid "kdesktop"
msgstr "Kdesktop"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; desktop"
msgstr "ផ្ទៃតុ KDE"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kicker;"
msgstr "Kicker"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:926
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; panel"
msgstr "បន្ទះ KDE"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid "ktip"
msgstr "Ktip"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:932
#, no-c-format
msgid "A tip of the day program"
msgstr "ព័ត៌មាន​នៃ​កម្មវិធី​ថ្ងៃ"

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid "kwrited"
msgstr "Kwrited"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:938
#, no-c-format
msgid "A utility to receive system messages sent to the user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:943
#, no-c-format
msgid "&klipper;"
msgstr "Klipper"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:944
#, no-c-format
msgid "A clipboard utility that docks in the panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: command
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:949
#, no-c-format
msgid "kalarm"
msgstr "Kalarm"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid "A utility that warns about upcoming events and appointments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:956
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdesktop</command> in its turn automatically starts applications "
"stored in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>"
"/Autostart</filename>. <command>kdesktop</command> will automatically open any "
"files stored in this directory including documents, binary files or "
"applications in the form of <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; session manager also restores one of the previous sessions. A session "
"contains a collection of applications as well as application-specific "
"information that reflects the state of the applications at the time the session "
"was saved. Sessions are stored in the <filename>ksmserverrc</filename> "
"configuration file which contains references to application-specific state "
"information. The application-specific state information is saved in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/share/config/session</filename>"
". The state information of &kwin; contains the location of the application "
"windows of all the other applications in the session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:978
#, no-c-format
msgid "Environment variables"
msgstr "អថេរ​បរិស្ថាន"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some important environment variables used by &kde;:"
msgstr "អថេរ​បរិស្ថាន​សំខាន់​ខ្លះ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដោយ KDE ៖"

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:986
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Has to be set if <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> is not set and has to point to the root "
"of the &kde; installation tree. Allows &kde; to find its data like icons, menus "
"and libraries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:993
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEDIRS</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEDIRS</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:994
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Overrides <envar>KDEDIR</envar> and allows you to specify multiple directories "
"where &kde; searches for its data. Useful if you want or have to install some "
"programs to a different prefix than the rest of &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: envar
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid "$KDEHOME"
msgstr "$KDEHOME"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not set, &kde; uses <filename class=\"directory\">~/.kde</filename> "
"as the directory where personal data is stored."
msgstr ""
"បើ​មិន​កំណត់ KDE ប្រើ <filename class=\"directory\">~/.kde</filename> "
"ជា​ថត​ដែល​ទិន្នន័យ​ផ្ទាល់ខ្លួន​ត្រូវ​បាន​រក្សា​ទុក ។"

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEROOTHOME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEROOTHOME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1007
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If not set, &kde; uses <filename class=\"directory\">~root/.kde</filename> "
"as the directory for <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>"
"'s personal data. Was introduced to prevent &kde; from accidently overwriting "
"user data with root permissions when the user runs a &kde; program after "
"switching with <command>su</command> to <systemitem class=\"username\">"
"root</systemitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1017
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEWM</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEWM</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1017
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <envar>KDEWM</envar> environment variable has been set, then it will be "
"used as &kde;'s window manager within the <command>startkde</command> "
"script instead of &kwin;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_LANG</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_LANG</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Overrides the &kde; language configuration, &eg; <userinput>"
"KDE_LANG=fr kprogram &amp;</userinput> starts a program with French translation "
"if the necessary files are installed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1031
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_MULTIHEAD</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_MULTIHEAD</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1031
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set this variable to <literal>true</literal> to indicate that &kde; is running "
"on a multi-head system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_FORK_SLAVES</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_FORK_SLAVES</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1038
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2.3) Set this variable to spawn <acronym>KIO</acronym>"
"-slaves directly from the application process itself. By default <acronym>"
"KIO</acronym>-slaves are spawned using <command>klauncher</command>/<command>"
"kdeinit</command>. This option is useful if the <acronym>KIO</acronym>"
"-slave should run in the same environment as the application. This can be the "
"case with <application>Clearcase</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1048
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_HOME_READONLY</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_HOME_READONLY</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1049
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set this variable to indicate that your home directory is mounted as read-only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_NO_IPV6</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_NO_IPV6</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2.3) - Set this variable to disable <acronym>IPv6</acronym> "
"support and <acronym>IPv6</acronym> <acronym>DNS</acronym> lookups."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_IS_PRELINKED</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_IS_PRELINKED</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1061
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) - Set this variable to indicate that you have prelinked your "
"&kde; binaries and libraries. This will turn off <command>kdeinit</command>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_UTF8_FILENAMES</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_UTF8_FILENAMES</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1068
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this environment variable is set, &kde; assumes all filenames are in "
"<acronym>UTF-8</acronym> encoding regardless of the current C locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDE_FULL_SESSION</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDE_FULL_SESSION</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Automatically set to true by &kde; startup, it is used by "
"&eg; &konqueror; to know if it should consider remaining in memory for future "
"re-use when being closed. If not set, &konqueror; will exit after being closed "
"(&eg; &kdesu; does that, it's also useful for debugging)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDESYCOCA</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDESYCOCA</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1084
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows you to specify the path and the name of the generated &kde; system "
"configuration cache file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1090
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDETMP</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDETMP</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1090
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows to specify another path than <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/tmp</filename> where &kde; stores its temporary files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1097
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>KDEVARTMP</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>KDEVARTMP</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1097
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Allows to specify another path than <filename class=\"directory\">"
"/var/tmp</filename> where &kde; stores its variable files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Defines the base directory relative to which user-specific "
"data files should be stored. Default is <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"HOME</envar>/.local/share</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1111
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(Since &kde; 3.2) Defines the preference-ordered set of base directories to "
"search for data files in addition to the <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"XDG_DATA_HOME</envar></filename> base directory. Default is <literal>"
"/usr/local/share/:/usr/share/</literal>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; adds locations from $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> and profiles as well. Used "
"for <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> and <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.directory</literal> menu files. <literal role=\"extension\">"
".desktop</literal> files under <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>/applications</filename>. <literal role=\"extension\">"
".directory</literal> files under $XDG_DATA_DIRS/desktop-directories"
msgstr ""
"KDE បន្ថែម​ទីតាំង​ពី $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> និង​ទម្រង់​ផង​ដែរ ។ "
"ដែល​ប្រើ​សម្រាប់ <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"និង​ឯកសារ​ម៉ឺនុយ <literal role=\"extension\">.directory</literal> "
"។ ឯកសារ <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"នៅ​ពី​ក្រោម <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>"
"/applications</filename> ។ ឯកសារ <literal role=\"extension\">"
".directory</literal> នៅ​ពី​ក្រោម $XDG_DATA_DIRS/desktop-directories"

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(&kde; 3.2) - Defines the base directory relative to which user specific "
"configuration files should be stored. Default is <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>HOME</envar>/.config</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</envar>"
msgstr "$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</envar>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(&kde; 3.2) - Defines the preference-ordered set of base directories to search "
"for configuration files in addition to the $<envar>XDG_CONFIG_HOME</envar> "
"base directory. The default is <filename class=\"directory\">/etc/xdg</filename> "
"&kde; adds locations from $<envar>KDEDIRS</envar> and profiles as well. Used by "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.menu</literal> descriptions in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$<envar>XDG_CONFIG_DIRS</envar>/menus</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1151
#, no-c-format
msgid "The kdeinit Mystery"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdeinit</command> is used to start all other &kde; programs. <command>"
"kdeinit</command> can start normal binary program f iles as well as <command>"
"kdeinit</command> loadable modules (<acronym>KLM</acronym>s). <acronym>"
"KLM</acronym>s work just like binary program files but can be started more "
"efficiently. <acronym>KLM</acronym>s live in <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/lib/kde3</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>ps aux | grep bastian</command>"
"</userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"bastian  26061  0.0  2.2 24284 11492 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"Running...\n"
"bastian  26064  0.0  2.2 24036 11524 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"dcopserver\n"
"bastian  26066  0.1  2.5 26056 12988 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klauncher\n"
"bastian  26069  0.4  3.2 27356 16744 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: kded\n"
"bastian  26161  0.2  2.7 25344 14096 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"ksmserver\n"
"bastian  26179  1.1  3.4 29716 17812 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: kicker\n"
"bastian  26192  0.4  3.0 26776 15452 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klipper\n"
"bastian  26195  1.0  3.5 29200 18368 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"kdesktop\n"
"</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>ps aux | grep bastian</command>"
"</userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>\n"
"bastian  26061  0.0  2.2 24284 11492 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"Running...\n"
"bastian  26064  0.0  2.2 24036 11524 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"dcopserver\n"
"bastian  26066  0.1  2.5 26056 12988 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klauncher\n"
"bastian  26069  0.4  3.2 27356 16744 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: kded\n"
"bastian  26161  0.2  2.7 25344 14096 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"ksmserver\n"
"bastian  26179  1.1  3.4 29716 17812 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: kicker\n"
"bastian  26192  0.4  3.0 26776 15452 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"klipper\n"
"bastian  26195  1.0  3.5 29200 18368 ?       S    21:27   0:00 kdeinit: "
"kdesktop\n"
"</computeroutput>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you might have noticed, this has another side effect, making it difficult to "
"kill a process that is causing trouble:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>killall kdesktop</command></userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>kdesktop: no process killed</computeroutput>"
msgstr ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>killall kdesktop</command></userinput>\n"
"<computeroutput>kdesktop ៖ គ្មាន​ដំណើរ​ការ​ដែល​បាន​ពិឃាដ</computeroutput>"

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You might be tempted to try <userinput><command>killall kdeinit</command>"
"</userinput>, but killing all kdeinit processes will have the effect of "
"shutting down all of &kde;. In effect, total destruction!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1180
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two simple solutions to this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kdekillall kdesktop</command></userinput>"
"\n"
"or good old\n"
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kill 26195</command></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kdekillall</command> is part of the &kde; <acronym>SDK</acronym> "
"package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1191
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customizing &kde;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1195
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Desktop Icons</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1197
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde; uses several types of icons:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1199
#, no-c-format
msgid "Documents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Links to Websites (using <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Links to Applications (using <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"file)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Devices - Disks, Partitions &amp; Peripherals:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Explicit using <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic via devices:// io-slave"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1214
#, no-c-format
msgid "Vendor-specific (&eg; &SuSE;'s My Computer)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Websites"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1220
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Links to Websites using <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"file: <menuchoice><guimenu>Create New</guimenu><guisubmenu>File</guisubmenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Link to Location (URL)</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
". Change Icon using <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> dialogs. The resulting "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[Desktop Entry]\n"
"Encoding=UTF-8\n"
"Icon=/opt/kde3/share/apps/kdesktop/pics/ksslogo.png\n"
"Type=Link\n"
"URL=http://www.kde.org/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Applications"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1234
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Links to Applications using <literal role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> "
"file: <menuchoice><guimenu>Create New</guimenu><guisubmenu>File</guisubmenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Link to Application</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
". You must provide details yourself. Drag from &kde; Menu: Either copy or link "
"(creates symlink), much easier"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
