"The application with highest preference!. <filename>kview.desktop</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"InitialPreference=3\n"
"</programlisting> whereas <filename>kuickshow.desktop</filename> "
"contains <programlisting>\n"
"InitialPreference=6\n"
"</programlisting> Therefore, &kuickshow; will be used to open <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.gif</literal> files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1696
#, no-c-format
msgid "How can we make &kview; default?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A user can change file association in the &kcontrolcenter;. These changes are "
"stored in <filename>$<envar>HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/profilerc</filename>"
". To use the same settings for multiple users, store these settings in user "
"profile directory or the global &kde; config directory to use as default for "
"multiple users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1712
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Locking Down &kde;</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1715
#, no-c-format
msgid "How It Works - The Basics"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1717
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kde;'s lock down features are centered around the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1721
#, no-c-format
msgid "Make configuration options immutable"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1723
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restriction of specific actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1725
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict access to certain &URL;s"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1727
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict access to certain configuration modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1734
#, no-c-format
msgid "Immutable Configuration Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: subtitle
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1735
#, no-c-format
msgid "<subtitle>Locking Down &kde;</subtitle>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1737
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Immutable options allow system administrator to provide default settings that "
"can not be changed by the user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1740
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pre-existing configuration options of the user will be ignored once a "
"configuration option is made immutable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Options can be controlled either on a per entry basis, per group of entries or "
"on a file by file basis."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a file or group is immutable, all configuration options for that file or "
"group are immutable, even those options for which the system administrator has "
"no default provided."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1750
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The support in applications for immutable options may vary from application to "
"application. Although the user will not be able to make permanent changes to "
"immutable configuration options, the user may still be presented with an user "
"interface option to make such change."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1758
#, no-c-format
msgid "Action Restrictions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; applications are built around the action-concept. Actions can be "
"activated in various ways, typically via the menu-bar, one of the toolbars or a "
"keyboard shortcut. <action>Save Document</action> is an example of an action. "
"If you know the internal action name it is possible to restrict an action. When "
"an action is restricted it will no longer appear in the menu-bar or toolbar. "
"The internal name for the <action>Save Document</action> action is <option>"
"action/file_save</option>. The lock down framework also provides a set of more "
"abstract restrictions which can be used to disable functionality not covered by "
"a single action. An example is the <option>shell_access</option> "
"restriction which disables all functionality that would offer the user access "
"to a &UNIX; shell."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1773
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restrict User Access to Shells"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1775
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to prevent the user access to a command shell we can restrict the "
"<option>shell_access</option> action by adding the following to <filename>"
"kdeglobals</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1780
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE Action Restrictions]\n"
"shell_access=false"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since this affects the &kde; menu and the available applications, we must force "
"an update of the sycoca database:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1785
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>touch</command> <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
"/share/services/update_ksycoca</filename></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1787
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now re-login to &kde; and check the following points:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1790
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kmenu;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1791
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &konqueror;, <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Open Terminal</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1794
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>F2</keycap></keycombo> run command"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1799
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Full documentation about available actions can be found on <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.kde.org/areas/sysadmin/\">http://www.kde.org/areas/sysadmin/</u"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1802
#, no-c-format
msgid "A few of the more interesting actions are listed below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1806
#, no-c-format
msgid "action/options_configure"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Configure</guimenuitem> option form the <guimenu>"
"Settings</guimenu> menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1811
#, no-c-format
msgid "action/help_report_bug"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1812
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Report Bug</guimenuitem> option from the <guimenu>"
"Help</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1816
#, no-c-format
msgid "action/kdesktop_rmb"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1817
#, no-c-format
msgid "&RMB; mouse button menu on the desktop."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1820
#, no-c-format
msgid "action/kicker_rmb"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1821
#, no-c-format
msgid "&RMB; mouse button menu on the panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1824
#, no-c-format
msgid "user/root"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1825
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hide all actions or applications that require <systemitem class=\"username\">"
"root</systemitem> access."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1829
#, no-c-format
msgid "shell_access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1830
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hides all actions or applications that provide shell access."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1834
#, no-c-format
msgid "print/system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1835
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disables the option to select the printing system (backend)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1839
#, no-c-format
msgid "lock_screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1840
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether the user will be able to lock the screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1844
#, no-c-format
msgid "start_new_session"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1845
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether the user may start a second X session (see also &kdm;)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1849
#, no-c-format
msgid "opengl_screensavers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1850
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whether OpenGL screensavers are allowed to be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1854
#, no-c-format
msgid "manipulatescreen_screensavers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1855
#, no-c-format
msgid "Permit screensavers that do not hide the entire screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1863
#, no-c-format
msgid "&URL; Restrictions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1865
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are three types of restrictions that can be applied to &URL;s:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1870
#, no-c-format
msgid "list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1871
#, no-c-format
msgid "To control whether a directory listing is allowed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1875
#, no-c-format
msgid "open"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1876
#, no-c-format
msgid "To control whether certain &URL;s can be opened"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1880
#, no-c-format
msgid "Redirect"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1881
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To control whether one &URL; can open another &URL;, either automatically or "
"via a hyperlink."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1886
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Rules are checked in the order in which they are defined. The last rule that is "
"applicable to a &URL; defines whether the &URL; may be accessed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1890
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following rules disable opening http and https &URL;s outside <systemitem "
"class=\"domainname\">.ourcompany.com</systemitem>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1898
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE URL Restrictions]\n"
"rule_count=2\n"
"rule_1=open,,,,http,,,false\n"
"rule_2=open,,,,http,*.ourcompany.com,,true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first four commas skip over the selection criteria with respect to the "
"originating &URL;. This part is only needed with redirect type rules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1906
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>rule_1</option> forbids the opening of any http or https &URL;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1908
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>rule_2</option> allows the opening of any http and https &URL; in the "
"<systemitem class=\"domainname\">.ourcompany.com</systemitem> "
"domain. Note the wildcard <token>*</token> is only allowed at the start of a "
"domain."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1914
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following rules makes that the user can no longer browse directories on the "
"local file system that are outside his $<envar>HOME</envar> directory:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1922
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE URL Restrictions]\n"
"rule_count=2\n"
"rule_1=list,,,,file,,,false\n"
"rule_2=list,,,,file,,$HOME,true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1925
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>rule_1</option> forbids the listing of any local directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1927
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>rule_2</option> allows listing directories under the users own $<envar>"
"HOME</envar> directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1932
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$<envar>HOME</envar> and $<envar>TMP</envar> are special values to indicate the "
"users home directory and the &kde; temporary directory of the user, &eg; "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/tmp/kde-bastian</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1936
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The following rules makes that the user can no longer open local files that are "
"outside his $<envar>HOME</envar> directory:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1944
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE URL Restrictions]\n"
"rule_count=3\n"
"rule_1=open,,,,file,,,false\n"
"rule_2=open,,,,file,,$HOME,true\n"
"rule_3=open,,,,file,,$TMP,true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1947
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>rule_1</option> forbids the opening of any local file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1949
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>rule_2</option> allows opening files under the users own $<envar>"
"HOME</envar> directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1951
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>rule_3</option> allows opening files in the &kde; temporary directory "
"of the user. This is needed by certain &kde; applications that first download a "
"file or document to the temporary directory and then open it in an application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1958
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The redirection option controls whether documents from a certain location can "
"refer, either automatically or manually via a hyperlink, to a certain other "
"location. A set of default rules is present as a general security measure. For "
"example documents located on the Internet may not refer to locally stored "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1964
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, if we want to give the intranet-server <systemitem "
"class=\"systemname\">www.mycompany.com</systemitem> the possibility to refer to "
"local files we could add the following rule:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1968
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE URL Restrictions]\n"
"rule_count=1\n"
"rule_1=redirect,http,www.mycompany.com,,file,,,true"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1970
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Instead of listing a protocol by name, it is also possible to specify a whole "
"group of protocols. For that the following groups have been defined:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1976
#, no-c-format
msgid ":local"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1977
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Protocols that access locally stored information, examples are file:/, man:/, "
"fonts:/, floppy:/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1981
#, no-c-format
msgid ":internet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1982
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common internet protocols such as http and ftp"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1987
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Information about protocols is stored in <literal role=\"extension\">"
"*.protocol</literal> files stored in <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>"
"KDEDIR</envar>/share/services</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1992
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <option>Class</option>= entry defines the group a protocol is part of: "
"<userinput><command>grep</command> <option>Class=</option> <filename>$<envar>"
"KDEDIR</envar>/share/services/*.protocol</filename></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:1997
#, no-c-format
msgid "General rules:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2000
#, no-c-format
msgid "The :local protocols may refer to any other protocol"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2002
#, no-c-format
msgid "It's always allowed to refer to an :internet protocol"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2004
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not all protocols are part of a group, fish:/ for example."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2011
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Modules"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2013
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; has configuration modules to configure various aspects of the &kde; "
"environment. Configuration modules appear in the Control Center, in the "
"Configuration dialog of an application or in both."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2018
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The proxy configuration module appears in the Control Center but also as part "
"of the <guilabel>Configure Konqueror</guilabel> dialog in &konqueror;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2022
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Individual configuration modules can be started with <command>kcmshell</command> "
"<replaceable>module</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2025
#, no-c-format
msgid "To start the Proxy module use:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2027
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kcmshell</command> <filename>kde-proxy.desktop</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2029
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kcmshell</command> proxy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2032
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Not all applications use configuration modules, often the configuration dialog "
"is an integral part of the application itself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2037
#, no-c-format
msgid "All configuration modules are strictly speaking part of the &kde; menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The modules that are visible in the Control Center normally have a <literal "
"role=\"extension\">.desktop</literal> file in <filename class=\"directory\">"
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/applications/kde</filename> "
"and are sorted under the hidden <guimenu>Settings-Modules</guimenu> "
"menu by the <filename>kde-settings.menu</filename>, included from <filename>"
"kde-essential.menu</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2048
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kbuildsycoca</command> <option>--menutest</option> "
"2&gt; /dev/null | <command>grep</command> Settings-Modules</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2051
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Application specific modules normally have a <literal role=\"extension\">"
".desktop</literal> file under <filename>$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>"
"/share/applnk/.hidden</filename> which corresponds to the hidden .hidden menu, "
"included as a result of <markup>&lt;KDELegacyDirs/&gt;</markup>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2055
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><command>kbuildsycoca</command> <option>--menutest</option> "
"2&gt; /dev/null | <command>grep</command> .hidden</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2057
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kde; 3.3 it is possible to edit the Control Center with <application>"
"kcontroledit</application>. <application>kcontroledit</application> "
"works just like <application>kmenuedit</application>"
", changes for current user only. Use <application>kiosktool</application> "
"to make changes for everyone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2065
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Individual configuration modules can be disables by adding the following to "
"<filename>kdeglobals</filename>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2068
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE Control Module Restrictions]\n"
"<replaceable>module-id</replaceable>=false"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2069
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example, to disable the proxy module use"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2070
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[KDE Control Module Restrictions]\n"
"kde-proxy.desktop=false"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2071
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check the Control Center and the <guilabel>Configure Konqueror</guilabel> "
"dialog if the proxy configuration is still there."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2090
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Lazy Admin"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2134
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote Desktop Sharing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remote desktop sharing allows remote users to view and optionally control the "
"desktop of the current user. The remote user needs to be sent an invitation, "
"and it is possible to create a password protected standing invitation. This is "
"ideal for tech support teams or administrators to gain access to users desktops "
"in order to troubleshoot or remedy a problem or guide a user through a "
"procedure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Remote desktop sharing involves two applications: &krfb; (&kde; remote frame "
"buffer, a VNC server) and &krdc; (&kde; remote desktop connection; a VNC "
"client.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&krfb; can be used by any user to create and manage invitations. Invitations "
"create a one time password that allows the recipient to connect to your "
"desktop. By default it is valid for only one successful connection, and expires "
"after one hour if not used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Incoming connections are handled by the kinetd kded module. You can use the "
"command <userinput><command>dcop</command> kded kinetd services</userinput> "
"to see if it is running. &krfb; waits for connections on port 5900 by default. "
"When an incoming connection is made, a dialog will appear to ask for "
"confirmation by the current user."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2163
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>&kde; DIY - Building Your Own Tools</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2166
#, no-c-format
msgid "DCOP"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Desktop COmmunication Protocol, <acronym>DCOP</acronym>"
", is a lightweight mechanism for inter-process communication. <acronym>"
"DCOP</acronym> allows the user to interact with programs that are currently "
"running. &kde; supplies two programs to utilitize <acronym>DCOP</acronym>"
": <application>dcop</application>, a command-line program, and <application>"
"kdcop</application>, a <acronym>GUI</acronym> program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2175
#, no-c-format
msgid "A few notes about using <command>dcop</command>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: kde-for-admins.docbook:2182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
